                  If any ſhallshall kill his parent, let him not be put to the ſwordsword, nor fire, nor any other vſuallusual puniſhmentpunishment: but let him be ſowedsowed in a ſackesack with a dog, and a cockecock, and a viper, and an ape, and caſtcast into the next ſeasea, or riuerriver; that while life is in him, he may begin to want all vſeuse of the elements, and be depriueddeprived, while he liuethliveth, of the aireair, and when he is dead, of the earth.
